title op3: renaming a directory over a hard-linked pair

# The OP3/OP6 composition, and the one fixture of the ten whose old
# behaviour destroys something silently.
#
# Pool 5 holds two names, /d/a and /d/b, both inside /d.  Off-of runs
# one command -- mv d e -- and touches nothing else.  Onto is quiet.
#
# Under full-path naming the pool loses TWO names and gains TWO.
# Definition 9.3 pairs a gained name with a lost one only in the
# one-lost one-gained case and degrades everything else, so the gains
# become attachments; and with the other side quiet, that degrade is
# what makes the pool materialize instead of keeping its dnode
# (op6-identity-cost.md).  A hard-linked pair loses its identity --
# onto-side links and open handles with it -- because somebody
# renamed the folder above it.  Nothing in the report says so.
#
# Relativized: (base /d, off-of /e) corresponds by red, and inside
# the pair the leaves a and b are unchanged.  The pool lost nothing
# and gained nothing, so no succession question is asked and there is
# nothing to degrade.  Section 16 removes this source of multi-loss
# outright; the remaining source -- a pool whose OWN links were
# renamed together -- is what op6-set-succession.md addresses, and
# that document is still PENDING the lead.
#
# Hand-worked: clean, dnode 5 kept, both names still on it.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: d/
      5-100: a = v0
      5-100: b

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: d/
      5-100: a = v0
      5-100: b

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: e/
      5-100: a = v0
      5-100: b

#
# WORKED OUTCOME (by hand, before any implementation ran)
#   believed moves:  none needed; red corresponds (base /d, /e)
#   deltas:          pool 5 lost nothing and gained nothing relative
#                    to the pair.  Under full-path reading it lost
#                    {/d/a, /d/b} and gained {/e/a, /e/b} -- the
#                    multi-loss that degraded and destroyed identity
#   decisions:       the directory renames d to e; pool 5 keeps its
#                    dnode and both of its names
#   conflicts:       none, onto is quiet
#   emission:        one rename, of the directory
# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect clean

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: e
      5-100: a = v0
      5-100: b
